    "28": {
      "date": "2026-09-27",
      "edition": "Sunday 27 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Log standings",
          "heading": "Fiji languish at bottom of Nations Championship table after Scotland defeat",
          "body": "Fiji sit in 12th place out of 12 teams in the Nations Championship table. The Flying Fijians have suffered three defeats in their opening three tournament matches. They scored 49 points across those three fixtures. The defence conceded 145 points over the same matches. That leaves the team with a tournament points difference of -96. Their last outing resulted in a 17-33 defeat against Scotland in Round 3. It is a stark contrast to 2023, when the team reached their highest world ranking of No. 7."
        },
