    "388": {
      "date": "2026-09-27",
      "edition": "Sunday 27 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Team news",
          "heading": "Ireland women make six changes for Sunday fixture against Japan",
          "body": "Ireland head coach Scott Bemand has reshuffled his side for today's WXV Global Series encounter against Japan in Galway. Following last weekend’s defeat to the USA, Bemand has introduced Béibhinn Parsons, Anna McGann, and Aoibheann Reilly to the backline, while Eilís Cahill, Neve Jones, and Brittany Hogan join the starting pack. Aoife Wafer is ruled out due to a minor training injury. Bemand noted the matches against Japan and South Africa provide an opportunity to develop attacking prowess and technical cohesion."
        },
        {
