      "edition": "Sunday 27 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Legal verdict",
          "heading": "French court sentences two men for murder of Federico Martín Aramburú",
          "body": "A Paris court has concluded the trial regarding the 2022 death of former Argentina international Federico Martín Aramburú. Loik Le Priol was sentenced to 26 years in prison for the murder, while Romain Bouvier received 19 years for attempted murder. The court found that the two men, both former members of a far-right group, acted with a shared focus on violence. Aramburu, who earned 22 caps for Los Pumas, was killed following an altercation at a cafe in Paris."
        },
