    "465": {
      "date": "2026-09-27",
      "edition": "Sunday 27 September",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "WXV thriller",
          "heading": "New Zealand women lose to England following late Zoe Harrison try",
          "body": "The Black Ferns suffered a heart-breaking 26-19 defeat against England at Allianz Stadium on Saturday. Despite leading 12-7 at half-time through tries from Amy Du Plessis and Ayesha Leti-I'iga, New Zealand fell away as England capitalised on a second-half yellow card for Veisinia Mahutariki-Fakalelu. The scores were level at 19-19 late in the contest before Zoe Harrison’s interception try in added time ended New Zealand's eight-match winning streak. Captain Georgia Ponsonby highlighted the intensity of the encounter between the world's top two sides."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "467": {
